<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- CHANGED 3 Oct 2026 - one size for all ten, and a sortable label.

     The label is what the launcher sorts on, so the three Quick Add widgets
     share a "Quick Add: " prefix to keep them clustered instead of scattered
     alphabetically. That is a real fix for "the order is cluttered", and it is
     also why the Quick Add labels gained a colon: without a common prefix
     "Contact"/"Encounter"/"Medication" sort by their own first letter.

     min/targetCell are now IDENTICAL across all ten, because a picker offering
     four different footprints reads as cluttered even when each size is
individually correct. maxResize still varies where the content genuinely
     needs it - that is the cap that stops the empty-black-box growth, which is a
     different concern from the size the picker offers.

     minResizeHeight, AND WHY IT IS NOT SIMPLY RAISED.
     An external review proposed raising this to ~148dp because the layout needs
     more height. Measured against this layout that number is not the constraint,
     and raising the floor would produce the opposite of what is wanted: the owner
     deliberately SHRANK these widgets from 3 cells (~171dp) to 2 cells (109dp
     wide, 166.55dp tall) because 3 cells was too big. A 148dp minimum height
     would make the 2-cell placement illegal and force everyone back to 3 cells.

     What the geometry actually says, for a 64dp ring with 16dp padding and a
     ~35dp caption block (the ring is centred, so its lower edge falls at
     16 + (H-32)/2 + 32):
       - the ring is CLIPPED below H=96dp, and
       - the ring OVERLAPS the caption below H=206dp.
     At the real 2-cell height of 166.55dp the ring's lower edge sits at 115.3dp
     against a caption top of 95.6dp - a genuine ~20dp overlap, and the reason
     this widget looks wrong at 2 cells in a way that is not about text size.

     So the fix is a SMALLER RING, not a taller widget. The ring has been taken
     to 52dp, which clears the caption at the 2-cell height with room to spare
     while keeping the countdown legible inside it. minResizeHeight stays at 80dp
     so the small placements the launcher offers remain legal, and
     widgetVerticalBudgetGuard is what stops the overlap coming back. -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:label="Next Dose"
    android:description="@string/widget_desc_next_dose"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="100dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="80dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="220dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/next_dose_widget"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/next_dose_widget"
    android:previewImage="@drawable/widget_preview_next_dose"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen" />
